1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,000
Hey, let's all stay closer together.

2
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:09,580
This is a story that happened
right before I, Shinichi Kudo...

3
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,800
...was turned into Conan Edogawa.

4
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:20,660
You must be Shinichi Kudo, right?

5
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:22,900
About the recent
manga artist murder case...

6
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:25,640
...you did great for figuring out
the suspect's extremely ingenious trick!

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:28,180
Even Chief Inspector Megure
mentioned it!

8
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:41,220
You can say that Shinichi Kudo's
unusually sharp deduction skills...

9
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:48,060
...did help us solve the case.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,980
"Shinichi Kudo"
It's not a big deal.

11
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:02,220
I am a detective, after all.

12
00:01:02,980 --> 00:01:06,720
And, if it's Holmes, whom I respect...

13
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:11,720
...could surely have solved it
in half the time and effort I took.

14
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:13,420
Excuse me.

15
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:15,500
One last word, please.

16
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:18,260
I'm in a hurry, sorry.

17
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:25,360
He's so handsome!

18
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:28,080
Please look this way!

19
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:40,200
-Good morning!
-Morning!

20
00:01:44,740 --> 00:01:46,160
Ran, I can see your underwear.

21
00:01:46,600 --> 00:01:47,440
"Ran Mori"

22
00:01:47,740 --> 00:01:50,120
-Shinichi!
-It's light pink.

23
00:01:51,980 --> 00:01:54,360
I'm just kidding, I didn't see it.

24
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,420
So, how do you know
what colour I was wearing?

25
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,140
Just a simple deduction.

26
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:02,620
One...You turned 17 yesterday.

27
00:02:03,520 --> 00:02:07,980
Two...Your dad opened
the present from your mother...

28
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:10,080
...who's not living with you,
without asking.

29
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:11,540
My dad did?

30
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:14,840
I heard he told the master of
the café beneath your house.

31
00:02:15,140 --> 00:02:19,620
"Ran's too early to wear something sexy
like that, what's she thinking!", or something.

32
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:23,440
Third...You would immediately
wear the present she bought you...

33
00:02:23,940 --> 00:02:26,060
...because you love her.

34
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:31,900
Why is dad telling
people unnecessary things!?

35
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:37,280
But…

36
00:02:37,420 --> 00:02:39,300
You don't have to be so upset.

37
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:42,000
And I don't think your dad
meant you any harm.

38
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:50,180
And you are so popular, as usual.

39
00:02:50,500 --> 00:02:51,880
Help me, Ran!

40
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,900
You should clean up
your own mess, right?

41
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:58,440
You're so cold.
We're friends since forever, right?

42
00:02:58,880 --> 00:03:01,100
You're the cold one.

43
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:05,800
Lately you stopped
giving me birthday presents.

44
00:03:06,800 --> 00:03:09,640
You've never forgotten to get me
a present when we were younger.

45
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:13,840
Like 'Autobiography
of Sherlock Holmes'...

46
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:17,540
-...or 'Sherlock Holmes…'
-I don't know, okay,

47
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:20,700
I have no idea what a high school
girl would want for her birthday.

48
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:22,840
I want to go
to the amusement park!

49
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:25,740
-Tropical Land!
-Tropical Land?

50
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:28,220
We talked about it
the other day, remember?

51
00:03:28,520 --> 00:03:32,600
You said you'll buy anything I want
if I won the karate competition!

52
00:03:33,340 --> 00:03:35,080
I want to go to Tropical Land!

53
00:03:35,300 --> 00:03:37,660
No. We're not kids anymore.

54
00:03:38,080 --> 00:03:39,360
Both of you.

55
00:03:39,580 --> 00:03:41,640
You're having a couple's quarrel
first thing in the morning?

56
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:43,980
Don't say weird things.

57
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:46,980
Sonoko, Ran said she wants
to go to Tropical Land with you.

58
00:03:47,260 --> 00:03:49,660
I…!

59
00:03:50,340 --> 00:03:53,320
Will go with Sonoko.
Let's go, Sonoko!

60
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,540
We're going to be late.

61
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,640
Come on.

62
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:00,920
Why is she angry?

63
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:04,780
I understand.

64
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:11,260
This famous detective, Kogoro Mori,
will definitely find Shunsaku's whereabouts.

65
00:04:11,940 --> 00:04:15,140
Please imagine you're on a big wave.

66
00:04:17,240 --> 00:04:19,400
I mean on a big boat.

67
00:04:19,560 --> 00:04:23,220
Please, help me find Shunsaku.

68
00:04:23,700 --> 00:04:27,360
-This is his picture.
-Okay.

69
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:32,040
-Please be careful.
-Find him for me, please.

70
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,180
What Shunsaku?

71
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:44,560
This is not work to be done
by the great detective Kogoro Mori.

72
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:50,360
Ah, how could I forget!
It's time for Youko's appearance.

73
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:52,200
Yoko!

74
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:57,520
I hear that you're filming
a new drama series?

75
00:04:57,900 --> 00:05:02,040
Yes. I will take on a role
as a detective for the first time.

76
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,440
So please watch it!

77
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,260
Yoko as a detective?

78
00:05:07,660 --> 00:05:10,840
I heard you used someone
as the model of your character.

79
00:05:11,940 --> 00:05:13,060
-Yes.
-To get into your role.

80
00:05:13,240 --> 00:05:18,220
-That is the famous detective…
-That is the famous detective…

81
00:05:18,500 --> 00:05:21,700
-Kogoro Mori.
-Shinichi Kudo!

82
00:05:23,120 --> 00:05:27,280
I'm a big fan of his.
I wish I could meet him just once.

83
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:30,800
Damn!

84
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:35,320
Curse that detective brat.
Gaining popularity all the time…!

85
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:39,580
I'm soaked!

86
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:41,660
Please don't forget anything.

87
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:47,440
And also, Mr. Tatsumi will be in
the hospital longer than expected.

88
00:05:47,760 --> 00:05:52,600
So, I will be following you
to your trip tomorrow.

89
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:56,420
-Kitajima will be following us.
-I'm worried.

90
00:05:57,260 --> 00:05:59,980
So everyone,
have a sense of responsibility...

91
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:01,500
A trip…

92
00:06:02,040 --> 00:06:06,680
As student of Teitan High School,
and have a fun trip.

93
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:11,280
I want you to write a report of your
group activities and submit it...

94
00:06:11,420 --> 00:06:13,720
...so please take important notes.

95
00:06:13,760 --> 00:06:14,900
That's all.

96
00:06:15,180 --> 00:06:17,860
Any question?

97
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:36,360
"Challenge letter to Shinichi Kudo"

98
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:45,460
I can't wait!

99
00:06:46,700 --> 00:06:51,680
We haven't been on a trip
since our primary school trip, right?

100
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:57,660
Tomorrow we're going to the
art museum and then, Ashinoko.

101
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:02,120
And for the free time at night…

102
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:05,300
Shinichi, do you want
to go anywhere?

103
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:09,200
Shinichi!

104
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:14,400
I'm not joining the trip.

105
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:17,560
-Why not?
-It's a waste of time.

106
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:22,140
It's much useful to study a real case...

107
00:07:22,460 --> 00:07:26,300
...no matter if it's a human
relationships or society as a whole.

108
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:29,920
So, you go have fun.

109
00:07:31,320 --> 00:07:33,640
Shinichi.

110
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,400
"Kudo"

111
00:08:01,620 --> 00:08:03,180
"Challenge letter to Shinichi Kudo"

112
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:26,640
Interesting.

113
00:08:35,160 --> 00:08:37,140
"Shinichi Kudo, Shun Oguri"

114
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:41,960
"Ran Mori, Tomoka Kurokawa"

115
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:48,240
"Kogoro Mori, Takanori Jinnai"

116
00:08:48,460 --> 00:08:52,480
"Challenge letter to Shinichi Kudo"
"Prologue Until Their Goodbye"

117
00:09:11,620 --> 00:09:13,960
Good morning.

118
00:09:17,240 --> 00:09:20,560
-Good morning, Ran.
-Good morning.

119
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,900
Sonoko, what's that?

120
00:09:23,180 --> 00:09:26,200
Clothes, make up,
and my lucky lingerie.

121
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:27,620
Lucky lingerie?

122
00:09:27,820 --> 00:09:30,800
I'll have a boyfriend
by the end of the trip.

123
00:09:31,020 --> 00:09:34,520
Your passion towards love
is really something.

124
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:38,720
What are you talking about?
You are getting one too.

125
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:44,040
I don't know what so great about
detective mania, but he is very popular.

126
00:09:44,280 --> 00:09:49,540
So you will have to declare to them
that you're his wife in this trip.

127
00:09:50,660 --> 00:09:52,620
What's wrong, Ran?

128
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:56,180
-But Shinichi's not coming.
-Eh? Why?

129
00:09:56,640 --> 00:09:59,660
He said that school trips
are a waste of time.

130
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,120
That idiot.

131
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:05,180
Everyone, listen here.

132
00:10:06,360 --> 00:10:11,000
This is your tour conductor,
Miss Nishida.

133
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,500
"Tour Conductor, Mai Nishida"
I am Mai Nishida.

134
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:15,540
I will be your guide
for the next three days.

135
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:18,240
She's gorgeous!
So hot.

136
00:10:18,460 --> 00:10:23,220
-Please teach me everything, Miss Mai!
-We're departing. It's time to depart.

137
00:10:23,500 --> 00:10:25,300
Wait a moment!

138
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:33,320
-Sorry, Mr. Kitajima. I overslept.
-I'm glad you could make it.

139
00:10:38,340 --> 00:10:40,540
Alright everyone,
get in lines and board the bus!

140
00:10:41,120 --> 00:10:44,420
-Yes!
-I'm sitting in front!

141
00:10:44,600 --> 00:10:47,240
What's this?
You said you're not coming.

142
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,000
I changed my mind.

143
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:54,020
I think that it's not bad to have fun
like a kid once in a while.

144
00:10:54,380 --> 00:10:56,260
You're a kid too, right?

145
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:58,380
Isn't this a good thing?

146
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:02,260
So you can go to your
honeymoon together.

147
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:04,160
Sonoko!

148
00:11:13,020 --> 00:11:15,620
<i>A challenge letter to Shinichi Kudo.</i>

149
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:21,820
<i>I will kidnap one of your
classmates during your school trip.</i>

150
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:24,600
<i>If you can protect them, you win.</i>

151
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:28,200
<i>If you can't, I win.</i>

152
00:11:29,340 --> 00:11:31,240
<i>And when that happens...    </i>

153
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:34,820
<i>...you have to give up from
your High School Detective title.</i>

154
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:39,380
<i>This is a one-on-one fight
between you and me.</i>

155
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:43,820
<i>But I will give you one hint.</i>

156
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:46,420
<i>It will happen on the boat.</i>

157
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,920
"Kidnapper"

158
00:11:57,220 --> 00:11:59,220
That's awesome!

159
00:12:04,780 --> 00:12:08,880
Look at this!
So beautiful!

160
00:12:09,480 --> 00:12:11,360
Shinichi!

161
00:12:11,740 --> 00:12:13,740
Hey!

162
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:17,380
Welcome 2B class
from the Teitan High School.

163
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:19,440
I am Azuma, your captain.

164
00:12:19,700 --> 00:12:23,360
We will be explaining
emergency procedures...

165
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:26,140
...so please gather at the front deck.

166
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:29,520
-Hello everyone.
-Hello.

167
00:12:29,720 --> 00:12:32,100
I am Minamida,
pleased to meet you.

168
00:12:32,620 --> 00:12:36,780
In case of an emergency,
please put on the life jacket.

169
00:12:37,880 --> 00:12:40,100
Isn't he handsome?

170
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:42,720
Like a grown up man.

171
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:45,440
I've decided on him.

172
00:12:45,680 --> 00:12:50,220
-I'm going to get him.
-After you put it through your hands…

173
00:12:50,520 --> 00:12:54,620
This ship will go around the lake,
which will take about 1 hour.

174
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:58,380
So, please enjoy the lakeside sceneries.

175
00:12:58,980 --> 00:13:00,840
Yes.

176
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:04,940
This boat will become
a closed room for the next hour.

177
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:08,100
Come from wherever you want.

178
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:12,540
I will protect all of them.

179
00:13:22,020 --> 00:13:25,680
You're Shinichi Kudo, right?
That high school detective.

180
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:29,360
-Yes.
-I'm your fan.

181
00:13:29,900 --> 00:13:32,060
I'm so glad I could meet you.

182
00:13:40,380 --> 00:13:43,600
Mr. Minamida,
do you have a girlfriend?

183
00:13:43,780 --> 00:13:46,860
Sorry, but I have work to do.

184
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:49,200
Wait.

185
00:13:49,820 --> 00:13:52,040
I will not let you go.

186
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:55,520
50 minutes left.

187
00:13:56,140 --> 00:13:59,380
The ship is cruising at 20km/h.

188
00:13:59,820 --> 00:14:03,920
It's nearly impossible to approach
this ship without being noticed.

189
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:11,120
If I am the Kidnapper,
I should already be on this boat.

190
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:20,180
The captain, Kunio Azuma.

191
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:23,300
The crew member, Kyosuke Minamida.

192
00:14:24,220 --> 00:14:26,660
The substitute teacher, Shingo Kitajima.

193
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:29,420
And the guide, Mai Nishida.

194
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:35,840
But, no matter
who the Kidnapper is...

195
00:14:36,080 --> 00:14:39,860
...taking one student
from this boat is impossible.

196
00:14:41,940 --> 00:14:44,080
How do you plan to do it?

197
00:14:53,680 --> 00:14:56,100
What's wrong?
You're looking scary.

198
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:58,140
Nothing.

199
00:15:00,180 --> 00:15:03,880
It feels good to be on the water.

200
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:07,440
Let's take a picture together.

201
00:15:09,100 --> 00:15:14,000
We used to take a lot of pictures
together, but none recently.

202
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:20,040
Say Cheese!

203
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:24,340
What's with that face?
Smile, Shinichi!

204
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,380
One more.

205
00:15:26,660 --> 00:15:28,580
No!

206
00:15:31,580 --> 00:15:33,480
Sonoko?

207
00:15:36,100 --> 00:15:38,100
I feel sick.

208
00:15:39,160 --> 00:15:41,020
You're seasick?

209
00:15:41,160 --> 00:15:43,980
Are you alright, Suzuki?
Are you alright?

210
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:48,360
Stop sexually harassing me.
I'm feeling worse.

211
00:15:48,920 --> 00:15:49,940
Sonoko.

212
00:15:50,820 --> 00:15:52,300
There's a room for you to lie down.

213
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:55,260
-Kudo, help me.
-Alright.

214
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:07,040
Thank you, Mr. Minamida.

215
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:10,960
<i>What about me?</i>

216
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,900
Medicine…

217
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:15,900
I should've brought some with me!

218
00:16:16,060 --> 00:16:18,300
Don't worry, I have some.

219
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,120
Here you go.

220
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:24,420
Please forgive me, Miss Mai.

221
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:27,600
Don't worry it is a part of my job.

222
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:30,140
Take this.

223
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:31,980
Damn...

224
00:16:32,280 --> 00:16:35,540
Which princess gets seasick
even though she takes a cruiser...

225
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:37,240
...all the time at home?

226
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:39,480
You have a cruiser at home?

227
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:41,040
She may not look like it...

228
00:16:41,200 --> 00:16:43,200
...but she's the daughter of
the Suzuki Financial Group. Right?

229
00:16:43,540 --> 00:16:45,660
You don't have to tell me that.

230
00:16:46,020 --> 00:16:48,800
Mr. Minamida,
can you stay with me?

231
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,320
Sorry, I have work to do.

232
00:16:51,860 --> 00:16:54,920
We'll stay with Sonoko.

233
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:57,660
<i>Me too? Alright then.</i>

234
00:16:58,190 --> 00:17:01,390
Don't push yourself too hard.

235
00:17:02,700 --> 00:17:04,430
Take it easy.

236
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:12,280
And there goes Mr. Minamida.

237
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:16,760
-Sonoko.
-Don't be angry.

238
00:17:17,130 --> 00:17:20,720
I'll be alright here.
Both of you should go too.

239
00:17:22,270 --> 00:17:26,510
You have to make some
good memories with Shinichi.

240
00:17:27,360 --> 00:17:29,470
Are you sure you're alright?

241
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:32,080
Stay here, and
don't move around, ok?

242
00:17:32,350 --> 00:17:35,230
Just go.

243
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:44,780
Sonoko, lock the door
from the inside.

244
00:17:45,960 --> 00:17:48,380
Don't open the door
to anyone except me.

245
00:17:49,080 --> 00:17:50,410
Why?

246
00:17:50,780 --> 00:17:54,000
You don't want anyone else
to see you vomiting, right?

247
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:56,760
Alright.

248
00:17:58,560 --> 00:18:02,330
-What did you tell her?
-Nothing, just told her to sleep.

249
00:18:03,630 --> 00:18:05,070
"Resting room"

250
00:18:14,910 --> 00:18:16,190
Excuse me.

251
00:18:17,280 --> 00:18:21,120
About the weather, it looks like
it will turn very bad soon.

252
00:18:21,530 --> 00:18:23,050
You're right.

253
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:26,010
And one of the students is taking
a rest in the resting room...

254
00:18:26,160 --> 00:18:27,660
...due to seasickness.

255
00:18:28,200 --> 00:18:29,960
I don't think it's anything serious.

256
00:18:30,970 --> 00:18:33,520
Is that so? Thank you.

257
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:59,880
Everyone, look this way.

258
00:19:00,970 --> 00:19:02,010
Can you see it?

259
00:19:02,220 --> 00:19:04,880
The Torii gates of
the Hakone Shrine in Ashinoko...

260
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:07,310
...was made in the year 757.

261
00:19:07,520 --> 00:19:09,240
I'm taking the picture.

262
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:12,400
-Yes, okay.
-Thank you.

263
00:19:12,520 --> 00:19:14,890
-Is it alright?
-Yes!

264
00:19:15,210 --> 00:19:16,440
I'm nervous.

265
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:18,490
30 minutes left.

266
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:22,360
What's wrong, Kidnapper?

267
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:28,780
You're strange today, Shinichi.

268
00:19:29,180 --> 00:19:31,600
Ever since we got
onto this cruise ship.

269
00:19:32,190 --> 00:19:33,930
No, I'm not.

270
00:19:34,440 --> 00:19:36,960
I can tell.

271
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,060
I can.

272
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:47,290
-What was that sound?
-I have no idea.

273
00:19:47,630 --> 00:19:49,440
Let's take a look.

274
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:07,120
Over there!
That's Sonoko's headband!

275
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:15,470
Don't tell me that Sonoko…
From here?

276
00:20:20,840 --> 00:20:22,300
Mr. Minamida.

277
00:20:22,460 --> 00:20:24,440
Please tell the captain
to stop the ship immediately.

278
00:20:24,880 --> 00:20:26,280
Alright!

279
00:20:35,440 --> 00:20:38,010
Please be safe, Sonoko.

280
00:20:43,710 --> 00:20:47,500
Sonoko… is not here.

281
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:54,910
Miss Suzuki?

282
00:20:55,600 --> 00:20:57,400
What happened here?

283
00:20:58,860 --> 00:21:01,580
I don't know.

284
00:21:02,170 --> 00:21:04,430
One of the life jackets
that were here is missing.

285
00:21:06,810 --> 00:21:07,870
Life jacket?

286
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:10,940
Then, did Miss Sonoko
really jump into the lake?

287
00:21:11,310 --> 00:21:12,970
It's too early to say that.

288
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:15,310
Mr. Kitajima and Mr. Minamida.

289
00:21:15,550 --> 00:21:17,200
Let's split up and search
around the boat.

290
00:21:17,470 --> 00:21:18,220
Okay.

291
00:21:18,350 --> 00:21:19,960
Captain, please contact
the guards around the area...

292
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:22,080
...and request for a search
near the shores.

293
00:21:22,400 --> 00:21:23,310
Alright.

294
00:21:23,420 --> 00:21:27,560
Miss Mai, please tell everyone
that there's nothing to worry about.

295
00:21:40,300 --> 00:21:42,650
<i>That door was properly
shut just now.</i>

296
00:21:46,830 --> 00:21:48,910
<i>Did it open because of a struggle?</i>

297
00:21:55,100 --> 00:21:56,620
<i>It's empty.</i>

298
00:21:57,020 --> 00:21:59,200
<i>One person can hide in here.</i>

299
00:22:00,240 --> 00:22:03,180
<i>Did the kidnapper hide in
here from the start?</i>

300
00:22:03,690 --> 00:22:05,820
<i>And attacked Sonoko
when she's alone?</i>

301
00:22:06,560 --> 00:22:10,010
<i>Then put the life jacket on her
and jumped into the lake together?</i>

302
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:13,550
We're now at the central
southern part of Ashinoko Lake.

303
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:15,130
Yes.

304
00:22:15,960 --> 00:22:18,200
I will bring the boat
to a jetty right away.

305
00:22:20,190 --> 00:22:22,120
Miss Suzuki!

306
00:22:29,720 --> 00:22:31,740
You heard a loud noise just now...

307
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:34,350
...but there's nothing wrong with
the boat, so you don't need to worry.

308
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:38,060
"Do Not Enter"

309
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:55,180
Anything there?

310
00:22:57,020 --> 00:22:58,750
Nothing.

311
00:23:03,930 --> 00:23:06,200
Let's look somewhere else.

312
00:23:13,630 --> 00:23:16,220
I was controlling the boat
from the control room.

313
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:19,020
I was at the boat's front deck.

314
00:23:19,400 --> 00:23:21,680
I didn't think that something
like this would happen…

315
00:23:21,840 --> 00:23:24,460
Don't worry, we'll take…

316
00:23:44,090 --> 00:23:45,680
Shinichi.

317
00:23:47,120 --> 00:23:49,260
Let's wait inside.

318
00:24:04,480 --> 00:24:06,200
Look at that!

319
00:24:13,880 --> 00:24:15,520
Call the headquarters, now!

320
00:24:16,060 --> 00:24:20,400
The kidnapped is Suzuki Financial
Groups' second daughter.

321
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:25,870
There's no contact
from the suspect yet.

322
00:24:26,140 --> 00:24:28,430
But there's high possibility
they will ask for ransom.

323
00:24:29,500 --> 00:24:35,530
Our mission is to find and ensure
the safety of Sonoko Suzuki!

324
00:24:46,220 --> 00:24:49,120
-Who are you?
-Shinichi Kudo.

325
00:24:49,960 --> 00:24:51,470
A detective.

326
00:24:52,040 --> 00:24:54,750
-Please let me join the investigation.
-A detective?

327
00:24:54,980 --> 00:24:56,340
Oh, oh!

328
00:24:56,430 --> 00:24:58,730
He's the one featured on the media.

329
00:24:58,890 --> 00:25:02,480
The kid that has been solving
several hard cases in Tokyo.

330
00:25:05,920 --> 00:25:08,800
I have no idea how great you are.

331
00:25:08,920 --> 00:25:12,920
-But this is not a place for an outsider.
-I'm not an outsider.

332
00:25:14,560 --> 00:25:17,040
Sonoko is an important classmate.

333
00:25:17,900 --> 00:25:19,920
Please contact Inspector Megure
from the Metropolitan Police.

334
00:25:20,160 --> 00:25:21,420
Let me join the investigation.

335
00:25:21,580 --> 00:25:23,470
I'm not going to listen to
the Metropolitan Police.

336
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:25,200
What are you all doing?!

337
00:25:25,580 --> 00:25:28,490
-Go investigate!
-Yes.

338
00:25:29,020 --> 00:25:30,300
Please wait.

339
00:25:32,010 --> 00:25:33,380
Please tell just one thing.

340
00:25:37,020 --> 00:25:38,760
How much oxygen was left
inside the tank that you found?

341
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:40,350
180.

342
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:42,540
-Why do you want to know?
-Nothing.

343
00:25:43,630 --> 00:25:45,400
Thank you.

344
00:25:56,270 --> 00:25:57,710
Hello, dad?

345
00:25:58,840 --> 00:26:02,830
What?
That rich brat was kidnapped?

346
00:26:03,040 --> 00:26:04,960
I'm just worried.

347
00:26:05,310 --> 00:26:07,630
She's your important friend.

348
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:10,110
I promise you that I'll find her.

349
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:12,920
I'm heading down there,
wait for me.

350
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:17,520
Hello, dad?

351
00:26:23,610 --> 00:26:26,620
Sonoko…

352
00:26:27,520 --> 00:26:29,710
Please be safe.

353
00:26:31,180 --> 00:26:32,880
Inspector Megure.

354
00:26:33,710 --> 00:26:37,840
I was not allowed to join
the investigation by the local police.

355
00:26:38,170 --> 00:26:39,770
I thought so.

356
00:26:40,090 --> 00:26:48,410
Tamagawa is 10,000 times more
hard headed and stubborn than me.

357
00:26:49,400 --> 00:26:50,860
And he is also known as...

358
00:26:51,130 --> 00:26:54,890
...the non-negotiable Mount
Everest of the Prefectural Police.

359
00:26:55,930 --> 00:26:59,710
-I'm sorry that I couldn't help you.
-It's okay.

360
00:27:00,240 --> 00:27:03,210
I'll manage with whatever I have.

361
00:27:07,240 --> 00:27:08,670
"Unknown Caller"

362
00:27:14,600 --> 00:27:15,800
Yes.

363
00:27:16,490 --> 00:27:18,670
Is this Shinichi Kudo?

364
00:27:19,950 --> 00:27:22,090
Kidnapper.

365
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:24,460
That's me.

366
00:27:25,450 --> 00:27:27,560
Sonoko better be safe.

367
00:27:28,170 --> 00:27:30,990
For now, she is.

368
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:33,950
Let me out of here, you fool.

369
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:38,840
But that was too easy.

370
00:27:39,240 --> 00:27:41,550
And I gave you a huge hint too.

371
00:27:42,360 --> 00:27:44,510
This is boring.

372
00:27:45,290 --> 00:27:49,340
So, I will take another one tomorrow.

373
00:27:51,850 --> 00:27:58,480
And since you're so useless,
I'll give you an even bigger hint.

374
00:27:59,930 --> 00:28:01,070
Tell me.

375
00:28:01,450 --> 00:28:05,260
Tomorrow's abduction
will happen at exactly 12 noon.

376
00:28:05,710 --> 00:28:07,790
Not earlier. Not later.

377
00:28:09,950 --> 00:28:11,550
Till then...

378
00:28:12,380 --> 00:28:17,100
I'll reveal who you are
and save Sonoko by then.

379
00:28:52,570 --> 00:28:54,330
Ran…

380
00:28:54,560 --> 00:28:56,920
They told you to wait at the hotel.

381
00:28:57,920 --> 00:29:00,320
They told you too, right?

382
00:29:02,120 --> 00:29:04,280
I'm surprised you knew I was here.

383
00:29:04,750 --> 00:29:09,120
I know you'd be
investigating Sonoko's case.

384
00:29:10,250 --> 00:29:12,940
And the only lead you have is here.

385
00:29:15,770 --> 00:29:17,550
Here you go.

386
00:29:18,040 --> 00:29:20,000
You didn't eat anything, right?

387
00:29:20,330 --> 00:29:23,950
I know that when you're immersed into
a case, you'll forget everything else.

388
00:29:27,150 --> 00:29:28,200
Thanks.

389
00:29:31,210 --> 00:29:33,160
Let me help you.

390
00:29:33,950 --> 00:29:37,390
-You're just going to get in the way.
-I want to do something.

391
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:39,370
For Sonoko.

392
00:29:40,840 --> 00:29:42,840
She's my best friend.

393
00:29:43,930 --> 00:29:46,000
If I'm in the same situation...

394
00:29:46,240 --> 00:29:48,600
...I think Sonoko wouldn't be
able to sit down and just wait.

395
00:29:49,380 --> 00:29:50,720
Damn...

396
00:29:50,990 --> 00:29:54,750
You can never change your mind once
you put your mind to it, since we're kids.

397
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,760
Did you find anything?

398
00:30:03,610 --> 00:30:07,790
Even if the suspects' footprints are here...

399
00:30:08,010 --> 00:30:09,640
...it would be wiped off by the rain.

400
00:30:10,330 --> 00:30:12,200
If...?

401
00:30:12,750 --> 00:30:16,380
The culprit took Sonoko here
from the lake, right?

402
00:30:17,120 --> 00:30:18,830
That's true.

403
00:30:19,340 --> 00:30:24,040
They found a man's wetsuit and
life jacket from the ship here.

404
00:30:25,120 --> 00:30:29,870
But, if this is a trick used
by the suspect…

405
00:30:30,160 --> 00:30:32,040
What do you mean?

406
00:30:32,880 --> 00:30:35,260
The amount left in the oxygen tank.

407
00:30:42,540 --> 00:30:45,160
If there's a chance Sonoko
did jump, it should be here.

408
00:30:45,770 --> 00:30:49,640
And the oxygen tank
was found here.

409
00:30:50,250 --> 00:30:54,860
Too much oxygen left in the tank,
even if they swam in a straight line.

410
00:30:58,480 --> 00:31:03,930
The suspect left the evidence
here in advance...

411
00:31:04,140 --> 00:31:08,490
...so that we would think that
it is done by an outsider.

412
00:31:10,810 --> 00:31:16,330
So, the suspect was
on the ship at the time?

413
00:31:19,160 --> 00:31:21,260
I have no idea.

414
00:31:21,600 --> 00:31:26,700
But, it looks like we have to
investigate the ship one more time.

415
00:31:31,280 --> 00:31:35,200
Let's go over what happened again.

416
00:31:38,270 --> 00:31:42,670
When we heard the sound...

417
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:46,480
Everyone was at the front deck.

418
00:31:46,890 --> 00:31:50,590
The captain,
Azuma was steering the ship.

419
00:31:50,970 --> 00:31:56,970
So it is impossible for anyone
on the boat to kidnap her.

420
00:31:58,520 --> 00:32:02,910
I bet someone was hiding
and kidnapped Sonoko.

421
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:09,500
No, those four is still suspicious.

422
00:32:16,650 --> 00:32:19,690
It's possible to create
an alibi using tricks.

423
00:32:32,220 --> 00:32:36,120
Trace of gunpowder...

424
00:32:36,320 --> 00:32:39,840
-Just as I thought.
-Gunpowder?

425
00:32:41,500 --> 00:32:46,160
For example, you tie
a weight using a rope here.

426
00:32:46,410 --> 00:32:50,940
And place a small ignition
device to burn the ropes.

427
00:32:51,080 --> 00:32:52,990
The weight will fall into the lake...

428
00:32:53,280 --> 00:32:55,920
...and create an illusion that
someone jumped into the lake.

429
00:32:56,910 --> 00:33:02,720
Meaning, Sonoko was kidnapped
before we heard the sound.

430
00:33:03,880 --> 00:33:05,920
Then where was she?

431
00:33:06,410 --> 00:33:08,860
She was not on the boat.

432
00:33:11,240 --> 00:33:17,520
Was she dumped in the lake and
we can never find her again?

433
00:33:18,800 --> 00:33:20,090
Right?

434
00:33:28,700 --> 00:33:30,410
Don't worry.

435
00:33:32,300 --> 00:33:34,440
Sonoko was safe.

436
00:33:35,900 --> 00:33:37,850
She was?

437
00:33:38,620 --> 00:33:42,060
What do you mean?
Shinichi!

438
00:33:45,480 --> 00:33:47,210
I'll confess.

439
00:33:50,620 --> 00:33:55,160
A challenge letter was sent to me.

440
00:33:56,700 --> 00:33:59,760
It was sent by the 'Kidnapper'.

441
00:34:01,070 --> 00:34:06,110
It wrote, "I will kidnap one of your
classmates during your school trip."

442
00:34:06,720 --> 00:34:11,070
And just now, I received a call from the suspect
about plans of a second abduction.

443
00:34:13,240 --> 00:34:18,410
He's going to kidnap another
student tomorrow at noon.

444
00:34:21,260 --> 00:34:25,790
When I received the phone call,
I heard Sonoko's voice.

445
00:34:29,660 --> 00:34:31,360
Ran?

446
00:34:33,020 --> 00:34:34,670
Why?

447
00:34:37,980 --> 00:34:41,790
Why didn't you contact the police
when you receive the challenge letter?

448
00:34:43,660 --> 00:34:45,760
These aren't games, you know?

449
00:34:47,050 --> 00:34:51,630
Detective should not put lives of
people around them in danger!

450
00:34:55,000 --> 00:34:57,210
I don't think this is a game.

451
00:34:59,420 --> 00:35:04,040
This is… a match between me and him.

452
00:35:04,140 --> 00:35:06,250
Match?

453
00:35:07,230 --> 00:35:11,130
Is there any point in having a match
with a coward like him?

454
00:35:11,260 --> 00:35:12,720
There is a point.

455
00:35:14,540 --> 00:35:16,840
It is because the suspect is a coward.

456
00:35:17,630 --> 00:35:21,840
If I run away from this...

457
00:35:22,110 --> 00:35:25,100
...he might do something
even worse the next time.

458
00:35:27,180 --> 00:35:29,210
It's written in the challenge letter.

459
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:35,960
If I break the one-on-one condition,
it could cause him to do something worse.

460
00:35:39,150 --> 00:35:40,960
And...

461
00:35:49,070 --> 00:35:51,950
And what?

462
00:35:53,800 --> 00:35:56,680
No. Nothing.

463
00:35:58,830 --> 00:36:00,440
Anyway, for now...

464
00:36:00,640 --> 00:36:02,800
...we need to think how to stop him
from executing the second crime.

465
00:36:03,480 --> 00:36:07,680
And to catch him during the act.

466
00:36:08,110 --> 00:36:09,880
That's all we can do now.

467
00:36:16,570 --> 00:36:19,550
Sometimes you should trust me, Ran.

468
00:36:24,080 --> 00:36:25,950
I trust you.

469
00:36:27,450 --> 00:36:36,140
But in exchange, no more secrets.

470
00:36:40,510 --> 00:36:43,770
Alright. I'll agree with that.

471
00:36:51,930 --> 00:36:54,160
As all of you know...

472
00:36:54,300 --> 00:37:01,800
A second kidnapping will happen
exactly at 12 noon today.

473
00:37:03,180 --> 00:37:04,960
So, we the prefectural police...

474
00:37:05,200 --> 00:37:07,780
...have discussed with
the school and as a result...

475
00:37:07,980 --> 00:37:11,280
...we have agreed that
it would be safer for you...

476
00:37:11,480 --> 00:37:14,170
...to be in this hotel
at the predicted time of crime...

477
00:37:14,440 --> 00:37:20,730
...than bringing you back to Tokyo.

478
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:32,200
So at noon,
everyone will gather in this hall.

479
00:37:32,750 --> 00:37:40,280
And we will lock all
five entrances from within...

480
00:37:40,680 --> 00:37:42,570
...and create a closed room.

481
00:37:42,960 --> 00:37:50,190
So, the kidnapper won't be able
to get close to any of you.

482
00:37:51,320 --> 00:37:53,070
Impressive.

483
00:37:53,440 --> 00:37:55,550
And...!

484
00:37:55,790 --> 00:37:59,790
There will be 5 policemen
standing outside each door.

485
00:37:59,930 --> 00:38:02,720
Furthermore,
there are policemen...

486
00:38:02,940 --> 00:38:07,600
...standing guard at every
usable entrance of this hotel.

487
00:38:08,700 --> 00:38:15,760
Meaning, you have 3 layers
of security guarding you.

488
00:38:16,350 --> 00:38:19,450
So I want you to be relaxed
and wait for noon to come.

489
00:38:20,400 --> 00:38:25,240
There's one more layer of security!
Let go of me, you fools.

490
00:38:25,420 --> 00:38:27,020
-Dad!
-Uncle.

491
00:38:27,150 --> 00:38:29,980
-Who do you think you are!?
-Sorry to keep you waiting.

492
00:38:30,320 --> 00:38:35,050
I am the famous detective,
Kogoro Mori.

493
00:38:35,580 --> 00:38:39,080
And I am also Ran's father.

494
00:38:40,160 --> 00:38:42,330
Another detective...?

495
00:38:42,620 --> 00:38:48,090
I will gladly help with
the investigation.

496
00:38:50,380 --> 00:38:54,640
A parent like should not butt in
an investigation like this.

497
00:38:54,860 --> 00:38:57,280
-But I am a famous detective.
-Everyone!

498
00:38:57,400 --> 00:38:58,480
Please return to your own room...

499
00:38:58,620 --> 00:39:02,540
...and return to this hall and
wait for us when you're ready.

500
00:39:02,700 --> 00:39:04,440
-That is all.
-That's all!

501
00:39:04,990 --> 00:39:07,360
You must wait!

502
00:39:07,560 --> 00:39:11,980
-Dad! You really came.
-Of course.

503
00:39:12,320 --> 00:39:14,520
How can I sit still
when you're in danger?

504
00:39:14,970 --> 00:39:18,250
That inspector doesn't let even me
to join the investigation.

505
00:39:18,620 --> 00:39:20,240
So I think it'd be
impossible for you too.

506
00:39:20,430 --> 00:39:23,520
Stupid police pride.

507
00:39:26,270 --> 00:39:28,080
I will be here to protect
everyone at noon.

508
00:39:28,350 --> 00:39:29,680
I want you to look
around the outside.

509
00:39:29,980 --> 00:39:32,120
But don't get in the way
of the guards, ok?

510
00:39:32,320 --> 00:39:34,730
Yes.
Don't tell me what to do!

511
00:39:34,880 --> 00:39:37,420
Dad, please take care of the outside.

512
00:39:37,920 --> 00:39:41,340
-It's for Sonoko.
-I know.

513
00:39:41,870 --> 00:39:44,090
I guess I'll leave the inside
to you, detective brat.

514
00:39:44,270 --> 00:39:48,460
-Ok, don't mess up.
-Stop talking to me like that.

515
00:39:51,950 --> 00:39:55,420
Alright. I'll go and take
a look around, first.

516
00:39:58,810 --> 00:40:02,490
I'll be checking this hall,
just to be safe.

517
00:40:03,370 --> 00:40:06,520
Ran, go rest in your room.

518
00:40:07,240 --> 00:40:09,500
You didn't sleep well since
yesterday night, right?

519
00:40:09,980 --> 00:40:11,470
Alright.

520
00:40:27,450 --> 00:40:29,850
Sonoko…

521
00:40:30,670 --> 00:40:34,030
Shinichi will catch the culprit soon.

522
00:40:36,120 --> 00:40:38,110
Just hold on till then.

523
00:40:44,750 --> 00:40:46,300
What's this?

524
00:40:51,960 --> 00:40:53,340
-Miss Fukuda?
-Yes.

525
00:40:54,510 --> 00:40:56,460
-Mr. Miyoshi?
-Yes.

526
00:40:56,920 --> 00:40:58,440
-Mr. Morimoto?
-Yes.

527
00:40:58,600 --> 00:41:02,010
Alright, so everyone's here.

528
00:41:18,170 --> 00:41:19,920
We're in the basement.

529
00:41:20,380 --> 00:41:25,080
The only 5 doors available
are locked from the inside.

530
00:41:25,800 --> 00:41:27,840
There are police stationed
outside the doors.

531
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:32,880
And only Inspector Tamagawa
has the master key to the doors.

532
00:41:35,950 --> 00:41:38,860
The air vents are too small
for humans to pass through.

533
00:41:41,370 --> 00:41:43,640
This time, it really is a closed room.

534
00:41:45,450 --> 00:41:49,420
So, where will you come from?

535
00:42:07,340 --> 00:42:09,980
This is the famous detective,
Kogoro Mori.

536
00:42:10,220 --> 00:42:13,020
Detective brat, the guard outside is perfect.

537
00:42:14,080 --> 00:42:16,670
I don't think even a mouse can get in.

538
00:42:17,280 --> 00:42:19,280
-It is perfect here too.
-Okay.

539
00:42:19,610 --> 00:42:23,450
But if something does happen…

540
00:42:24,780 --> 00:42:27,040
I'll leave Ran in your care.

541
00:42:29,400 --> 00:42:33,210
Damn, I didn't think I'd ever
need to say that line.

542
00:42:33,980 --> 00:42:37,020
I know, Uncle.

543
00:42:39,610 --> 00:42:44,120
In here, we only need to be
careful of one person.

544
00:42:55,720 --> 00:42:58,190
Everyone, gather around.

545
00:42:58,510 --> 00:43:00,350
-Teacher!
-Don't worry.

546
00:43:00,650 --> 00:43:01,980
You have nothing to worry about.

547
00:43:02,410 --> 00:43:04,800
-There's only 5 minutes left.
-Let's go quickly.

548
00:43:06,280 --> 00:43:08,510
It's okay.

549
00:43:08,760 --> 00:43:09,610
Don't worry.

550
00:43:09,800 --> 00:43:12,840
The culprit doesn't have to be a man.
She could be a woman too.

551
00:43:13,480 --> 00:43:17,530
Don't overlook the older people
and children too!

552
00:43:29,530 --> 00:43:33,520
Excuse me,
are you authorized to be here?

553
00:43:34,810 --> 00:43:39,420
I am Kogoro Mori,
the famous detective.

554
00:43:41,130 --> 00:43:42,440
I am Mai Nishida.

555
00:43:42,800 --> 00:43:45,440
I am the guide in charge
of the school trip.

556
00:43:45,740 --> 00:43:49,200
And I got caught in Sonoko Suzuki's
kidnapping incident and…

557
00:43:49,720 --> 00:43:51,920
So I'm worried about them.

558
00:43:55,580 --> 00:43:57,710
Mr. Azuma, Mr. Minamida...

559
00:43:58,060 --> 00:44:00,000
They are also people
who got caught in the incident.

560
00:44:00,110 --> 00:44:02,680
The ship's captain, Mr. Azuma.
And the crew member, Mr. Minamida.

561
00:44:03,120 --> 00:44:06,510
-This Mr. Mori, a detective.
-A famous detective.

562
00:44:07,150 --> 00:44:08,680
I couldn't just sit still...

563
00:44:08,940 --> 00:44:11,290
Thinking that something
could happen again.

564
00:44:11,690 --> 00:44:13,340
Don't worry.

565
00:44:13,550 --> 00:44:18,320
There's another bratty detective
inside there with them.

566
00:44:24,760 --> 00:44:28,780
Don't let go, no matter what.

567
00:44:30,830 --> 00:44:33,060
You have nothing to worry about!

568
00:44:42,730 --> 00:44:46,140
This is the corridor in front of
the main hall. All okay.

569
00:44:51,560 --> 00:44:52,970
It's alright.

570
00:44:55,980 --> 00:44:57,550
Don't worry.

571
00:44:58,280 --> 00:45:00,990
I won't let anything happen.

572
00:45:02,140 --> 00:45:03,640
Okay.

573
00:45:04,780 --> 00:45:11,740
But, I feel nervous every time I think
about what's happening to Sonoko.

574
00:45:14,810 --> 00:45:19,800
The only thing we should think about
is how two win this second attempt.

575
00:45:20,680 --> 00:45:22,490
That's all.

576
00:45:25,210 --> 00:45:27,050
You're right.

577
00:45:33,400 --> 00:45:38,520
It's nearly 12 noon.
Everyone stay at their position!

578
00:45:42,280 --> 00:45:46,940
Another 45 seconds left.
Kidnapper, bring it on!

579
00:45:47,340 --> 00:45:50,110
This Kogoro Mori will defeat you.

580
00:45:50,640 --> 00:45:53,370
Sorry, but I need to go
to the toilet.

581
00:45:54,140 --> 00:45:57,600
Me too, I need to make
a phone call.

582
00:46:00,440 --> 00:46:02,410
What are they doing
at a time like this?

583
00:46:41,660 --> 00:46:44,300
Everyone, calm down!
It's okay!

584
00:46:44,620 --> 00:46:47,420
The lights went out!
It's too dark to see anything!

585
00:46:47,680 --> 00:46:50,160
What, a black out? What happened?

586
00:46:50,400 --> 00:46:52,780
Get the power back up!
Get the power running quickly!

587
00:46:52,910 --> 00:46:54,560
Everyone stay at their positions!

588
00:46:54,800 --> 00:46:56,830
I wonder if they are all alright.

589
00:47:05,050 --> 00:47:07,160
Is everyone alright?

590
00:47:09,420 --> 00:47:11,480
Ran…

591
00:47:18,800 --> 00:47:20,780
Ran!

592
00:47:26,090 --> 00:47:27,960
Where is she?

593
00:47:28,250 --> 00:47:30,970
You suspect me?

594
00:47:32,030 --> 00:47:34,880
I was with these 2 the whole time.

595
00:47:35,150 --> 00:47:38,680
We were scared, so we held
onto him the whole time.

596
00:47:38,840 --> 00:47:40,570
Me, too.

597
00:47:57,920 --> 00:48:00,000
All the doors are still locked.

598
00:48:00,680 --> 00:48:03,000
What's the meaning of this?

599
00:48:14,110 --> 00:48:15,920
Ran!

600
00:48:27,290 --> 00:48:30,640
Ran!!!

601
00:48:31,840 --> 00:48:32,720
What's the situation there?

602
00:48:32,910 --> 00:48:34,910
-Tell me the situation there!
-Sorry.

603
00:48:35,230 --> 00:48:38,010
What?
A student disappeared?

604
00:48:38,460 --> 00:48:41,760
-What? What's happening?
-We don't have enough details yet.

605
00:48:41,930 --> 00:48:43,610
Uncle!

606
00:48:44,040 --> 00:48:45,120
What happened down there?

607
00:48:45,320 --> 00:48:48,040
I heard they say someone disappeared,
but the room was a closed room, right?

608
00:48:48,300 --> 00:48:53,040
-So how was she taken?
-What was the police doing?

609
00:48:54,140 --> 00:48:57,160
And…Who was taken?!

610
00:48:59,120 --> 00:49:01,530
Uncle.

611
00:49:07,070 --> 00:49:09,610
Ran disappeared.

612
00:49:11,770 --> 00:49:13,470
What?

613
00:49:16,200 --> 00:49:18,240
Shinichi!

614
00:49:18,540 --> 00:49:20,650
You useless!

615
00:49:24,010 --> 00:49:26,490
Didn't I tell you to take care of Ran?

616
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:31,400
I did, right?

617
00:49:33,340 --> 00:49:36,240
What are you doing?
Calm down!

618
00:49:36,380 --> 00:49:38,880
Let me go!

619
00:50:04,110 --> 00:50:05,950
How could you take Ran!

620
00:50:06,330 --> 00:50:07,900
It's my win, again.

621
00:50:08,700 --> 00:50:10,940
I guess you can't even
protect your friends...

622
00:50:11,100 --> 00:50:13,290
...even though the police
was on your side.

623
00:50:13,720 --> 00:50:17,840
Continuing a game like this
will get boring...

624
00:50:18,200 --> 00:50:19,710
...so this will be the last one.

625
00:50:20,350 --> 00:50:24,000
I have a bomb set at the place
where those two are kept.

626
00:50:26,000 --> 00:50:29,610
It will detonate at exactly
12 midnight, tonight.

627
00:50:30,540 --> 00:50:34,200
So, you think you can find it?

628
00:50:41,980 --> 00:50:44,590
12 hours left.

629
00:51:01,130 --> 00:51:02,730
Uncle.

630
00:51:05,160 --> 00:51:06,890
I apologize.

631
00:51:07,660 --> 00:51:09,680
For punching you.

632
00:51:10,300 --> 00:51:14,440
No, I need to thank you.

633
00:51:16,220 --> 00:51:19,690
I can't hit myself as hard as that.

634
00:51:23,020 --> 00:51:25,680
But what is going on with this case?

635
00:51:26,300 --> 00:51:28,640
Making a person
disappear easily like that.

636
00:51:29,820 --> 00:51:31,640
Is the suspect a psychic?

637
00:51:31,980 --> 00:51:35,930
The suspect's a normal person...

638
00:51:36,250 --> 00:51:39,000
...but with a deep shadow in his heart.

639
00:51:42,110 --> 00:51:43,960
I got another call from the suspect.

640
00:51:44,440 --> 00:51:48,410
He said that he set up a bomb at
the place he's keeping both of them.

641
00:51:49,530 --> 00:51:54,540
-The time limit is midnight.
-What?

642
00:51:54,670 --> 00:51:57,360
We have to find it, no matter what!

643
00:51:58,350 --> 00:52:00,520
But…

644
00:52:00,840 --> 00:52:03,600
We don't know the suspect's identity,
and how he does it.

645
00:52:03,930 --> 00:52:06,400
How do you expect to find him?

646
00:52:07,260 --> 00:52:09,920
And we have close
to zero clues to him.

647
00:52:11,050 --> 00:52:17,470
The only thing the police found was
that weird red ink on that door handle.

648
00:52:17,870 --> 00:52:19,800
Red ink?

649
00:52:20,320 --> 00:52:24,540
After the light turned back on, I ran out of that door to look for Ran.

650
00:52:25,120 --> 00:52:29,400
But I didn't notice any red ink
on the door handle back then.

651
00:52:29,880 --> 00:52:31,740
Then, does that mean
after you ran out...

652
00:52:31,900 --> 00:52:34,540
...one of the student touched it
and left the red ink?

653
00:52:35,760 --> 00:52:39,980
Then that will not be a good clue.
I guess all options are sealed to us.

654
00:52:41,370 --> 00:52:45,050
No, there are clues…

655
00:52:45,900 --> 00:52:46,970
You have an idea?

656
00:52:47,200 --> 00:52:50,440
Remember what Mr. Minamida
and Miss Mai said just now?

657
00:52:51,260 --> 00:52:53,950
I felt like one of them said
something weird.

658
00:52:54,440 --> 00:52:57,290
What is it? Do your best
to remember it, even if you'd die!

659
00:53:00,720 --> 00:53:04,560
-I heard they say someone disappeared.
-The room was closed, right?

660
00:53:04,840 --> 00:53:09,240
-So how was she taken?
-What was the police doing?

661
00:53:10,650 --> 00:53:14,620
Damn, what is it…
What feels off?

662
00:53:15,580 --> 00:53:18,640
At least I know that it is impossible
for Miss Mai to commit the crime.

663
00:53:19,020 --> 00:53:20,380
Why?

664
00:53:20,620 --> 00:53:23,200
She was with me the entire time.

665
00:53:24,080 --> 00:53:27,680
The entire time? Are you sure?

666
00:53:31,520 --> 00:53:33,920
The ones that are suspicious are...

667
00:53:34,120 --> 00:53:38,200
...the captain, Azuma
and the guy Minamida.

668
00:53:38,970 --> 00:53:40,440
Why do you think that?

669
00:53:40,890 --> 00:53:46,760
Minamida went to make a phone
call just before the blackout.

670
00:53:47,850 --> 00:53:51,980
And Captain Azuma
hasn't return from the toilet!

671
00:53:52,650 --> 00:53:56,490
That settles it.
The kidnapper is Azuma.

672
00:53:57,070 --> 00:53:59,980
He must be the suspect
for the first case as well.

673
00:54:01,020 --> 00:54:06,190
But, Mr. Azuma was steering
the ship when the first case happened.

674
00:54:09,390 --> 00:54:13,920
You're still young, so naïve.
It's on auto-pilot.

675
00:54:15,610 --> 00:54:18,650
Letting the ship steer itself,
he made an alibi for himself.

676
00:54:18,800 --> 00:54:21,070
In the meantime,
he went to kidnap Sonoko.

677
00:54:21,960 --> 00:54:23,520
How did he get Ran?

678
00:54:24,250 --> 00:54:27,420
You just have to catch him
and we'll know how he did it.

679
00:54:27,850 --> 00:54:29,710
We have no time, hurry!

680
00:54:39,980 --> 00:54:42,110
We're going in.

681
00:54:54,590 --> 00:54:56,220
Don't tell me…

682
00:55:05,130 --> 00:55:08,960
I knew it. He was the culprit.

683
00:55:09,390 --> 00:55:11,050
Damn it.

684
00:55:11,440 --> 00:55:14,960
We won't know
where Ran is if he's dead.

685
00:55:25,500 --> 00:55:29,180
Hey, why you just sitting there?
Help me!

686
00:55:30,270 --> 00:55:35,960
I wonder what does this arrow
on the back of this will.

687
00:55:38,810 --> 00:55:43,930
It's a bit dark, but it looks like
it's written with blood.

688
00:55:52,750 --> 00:55:55,340
Why is there a wound there?

689
00:56:07,920 --> 00:56:09,660
Uncle.

690
00:56:11,790 --> 00:56:13,960
He didn't do it.

691
00:56:14,410 --> 00:56:16,000
What?

692
00:56:18,300 --> 00:56:21,800
He was murdered by the real culprit.

693
00:56:41,500 --> 00:56:43,660
Sonoko, wake up.

694
00:56:49,290 --> 00:56:51,080
Ran.

695
00:56:53,840 --> 00:56:55,710
Let's run away.

696
00:56:58,060 --> 00:57:01,000
Anybody there? Help us!

697
00:57:01,480 --> 00:57:04,270
Anyone!?

698
00:57:07,880 --> 00:57:10,190
-This is the only door, right?
-Yes.

699
00:57:12,670 --> 00:57:18,090
-The only window are on the ceiling.
-What will happen to us?

700
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:21,340
Don't worry.

701
00:57:21,580 --> 00:57:24,830
I'm sure Shinichi will come save us.

702
00:57:34,350 --> 00:57:37,230
Actually, both of you an ideal couple.

703
00:57:37,740 --> 00:57:40,000
Shinichi and you.

704
00:57:42,250 --> 00:57:45,480
You're always fighting...

705
00:57:45,720 --> 00:57:50,720
...but you can still believe in each
other in situations like this.

706
00:57:51,070 --> 00:57:52,520
It's beautiful.

707
00:58:08,650 --> 00:58:11,290
That's a bomb, right?

708
00:58:12,830 --> 00:58:15,930
Are we going to die?

709
00:58:18,400 --> 00:58:20,120
Ran, that dangerous!

710
00:58:21,320 --> 00:58:23,900
I have no idea what to do.

711
00:58:25,200 --> 00:58:28,910
But it looks like we still have time.

712
00:58:33,360 --> 00:58:37,660
I wanted to fall in love
at least once before I die.

713
00:58:39,280 --> 00:58:41,680
Why are you talking like that?

714
00:58:44,600 --> 00:58:47,950
You can still fall in love,
as deeply as you want, after this.

715
00:58:48,220 --> 00:58:52,270
-You can't give up.
-But what can we do?

716
00:59:30,110 --> 00:59:33,120
-My leg hurts…
-You have to stop it.

717
00:59:33,920 --> 00:59:38,720
We won't be able to watch your
turning kick if you continue kicking like that.

718
00:59:40,590 --> 00:59:43,760
There's no point in me
learning karate...

719
00:59:43,950 --> 00:59:47,760
...if I don't use it
in situations like this.

720
00:59:48,400 --> 00:59:49,680
Ran…

721
00:59:49,820 --> 00:59:54,730
Shinichi will never give up
right till the end.

722
00:59:55,480 --> 00:59:57,400
Won't give up!

723
01:00:01,390 --> 01:00:05,310
Ran! That's enough.
Stop!

724
01:00:25,930 --> 01:00:28,960
-Ran!
-Ouch!

725
01:00:30,090 --> 01:00:34,350
-I think I cracked a bone in there.
-You think?

726
01:00:34,670 --> 01:00:37,400
How can you say that
with that cute face?

727
01:00:39,070 --> 01:00:42,920
Sonoko, let's go, hurry.

728
01:01:06,560 --> 01:01:10,120
-We can't.
-Why?

729
01:01:13,420 --> 01:01:15,150
What should we do now?

730
01:01:16,960 --> 01:01:20,760
I can't jump with my foot like this.

731
01:01:21,440 --> 01:01:23,960
Sonoko, you go.

732
01:01:24,880 --> 01:01:28,160
Tell Shinichi of this place.

733
01:01:29,180 --> 01:01:32,060
I can't. I can't jump down.

734
01:01:32,540 --> 01:01:35,560
And I can't leave you here all alone!

735
01:01:35,820 --> 01:01:40,270
If you stay here, both of us could die!

736
01:02:25,400 --> 01:02:26,780
Ran!

737
01:02:27,050 --> 01:02:31,920
I promise to bring Shinichi here,
so please wait for us!

738
01:02:46,030 --> 01:02:51,160
At least Sonoko is saved.

739
01:03:13,480 --> 01:03:16,110
Ran, sorry.

740
01:03:18,720 --> 01:03:23,310
Search Azuma's belongings
and find Ran's location, quickly!

741
01:03:23,600 --> 01:03:27,850
-There's a bomb that will blow up!
-We're in the middle of it!

742
01:03:28,190 --> 01:03:29,440
But!

743
01:03:30,030 --> 01:03:34,730
It looks like you've been snooping around,
so I hope you didn't take anything with you.

744
01:03:34,920 --> 01:03:36,280
Of course I didn't.

745
01:03:36,720 --> 01:03:38,600
I used to be an inspector!

746
01:03:38,920 --> 01:03:41,400
Preserving the crime scene
is the number one rule!

747
01:03:46,620 --> 01:03:49,200
What's wrong?

748
01:03:51,070 --> 01:03:52,430
Nothing's wrong.

749
01:03:58,970 --> 01:04:03,210
That Detective Brat, what is
he planning to do with the will?

750
01:04:04,910 --> 01:04:08,490
Inspector Megure, I need you
to check something for me.

751
01:04:13,210 --> 01:04:15,720
This is the most suspicious room.

752
01:04:58,920 --> 01:05:00,750
Just as I thought…

753
01:05:00,990 --> 01:05:03,880
Now I know how
they kidnapped Sonoko.

754
01:05:04,810 --> 01:05:08,800
There's no mistake,
that person did it.

755
01:05:10,140 --> 01:05:14,750
But, how did they kidnap Ran?

756
01:05:15,580 --> 01:05:20,800
The only thing the police found was
that weird red ink on that door handle.

757
01:05:21,930 --> 01:05:24,090
Ink on the door handle?

758
01:05:33,610 --> 01:05:35,530
Why is it on my hand?

759
01:05:36,510 --> 01:05:38,970
Sonoko's my best friend.

760
01:05:39,840 --> 01:05:42,010
If I'm in the same situation...

761
01:05:42,200 --> 01:05:45,450
...I think Sonoko wouldn't be
able to sit down and just wait.

762
01:05:49,500 --> 01:05:52,000
Don't tell me…

763
01:05:52,600 --> 01:05:56,670
But that would explain everything.

764
01:06:02,590 --> 01:06:04,270
This is Megure.

765
01:06:04,560 --> 01:06:08,380
-I got the result you asked.
-Alright.

766
01:06:10,650 --> 01:06:12,460
Understand.

767
01:06:13,440 --> 01:06:14,600
Thank you.

768
01:06:14,760 --> 01:06:16,380
And another thing.

769
01:06:19,710 --> 01:06:23,920
Kudo, I believe in you.

770
01:06:25,240 --> 01:06:27,000
So take care of them.

771
01:06:33,020 --> 01:06:36,730
An hour left.
Damn it!

772
01:06:41,240 --> 01:06:44,080
-Yes?
-Uncle, it's me.

773
01:06:44,400 --> 01:06:45,820
Where and what are you doing?

774
01:06:46,110 --> 01:06:47,850
I got a clue on where
they're keeping Ran.

775
01:06:48,000 --> 01:06:49,600
-Tell me.
-We'll talk later.

776
01:06:49,770 --> 01:06:51,020
There are 5 possible locations.

777
01:06:51,180 --> 01:06:52,680
We have to split up
and look for the place.

778
01:06:52,920 --> 01:06:54,590
Alright.

779
01:06:56,560 --> 01:06:58,490
Wait a second.

780
01:07:00,190 --> 01:07:04,440
-You are still here?!
-I have a clue to their location.

781
01:07:05,210 --> 01:07:06,160
Please look at this location.

782
01:07:06,360 --> 01:07:10,490
We will do things our way without
taking orders from anybody...

783
01:07:10,620 --> 01:07:14,840
...especially not from a detective.

784
01:07:15,050 --> 01:07:16,480
What?

785
01:07:17,530 --> 01:07:24,600
I'll show you the detective spirit that
doesn't rely on organizations and titles!

786
01:07:29,320 --> 01:07:30,880
Ran.

787
01:07:39,480 --> 01:07:41,160
Ran!

788
01:07:49,400 --> 01:07:52,030
Ran! Sonoko!

789
01:08:05,600 --> 01:08:08,780
Ran! Sonoko!

790
01:08:22,120 --> 01:08:23,900
It was you.

791
01:08:25,660 --> 01:08:29,210
Miss Mai Nishida.

792
01:08:36,890 --> 01:08:38,620
What a coincidence.

793
01:08:38,970 --> 01:08:40,840
Why are you here?

794
01:08:41,550 --> 01:08:45,420
Did you come to check on it?

795
01:08:46,510 --> 01:08:50,700
To check whether
the bomb is moving or not.

796
01:08:52,270 --> 01:08:53,800
Bomb?

797
01:08:54,410 --> 01:08:57,020
-What are you talking about?
-Don't play a fool!

798
01:08:58,080 --> 01:09:02,110
I want you to release
Ran and Sonoko.

799
01:09:04,810 --> 01:09:07,200
You're very rude.

800
01:09:07,800 --> 01:09:10,240
You're talking like
I'm the bad guy here.

801
01:09:10,590 --> 01:09:12,480
It bothered me all this time.

802
01:09:14,060 --> 01:09:18,350
The words you said,
just after the second kidnapping.

803
01:09:18,700 --> 01:09:21,850
So how was she taken?

804
01:09:22,200 --> 01:09:27,280
Back then, how did you know
that a female student was kidnapped?

805
01:09:28,620 --> 01:09:32,030
Even the police didn't have
any concrete information.

806
01:09:32,410 --> 01:09:36,280
-There's no reason to it.
-No, of course there is.

807
01:09:38,140 --> 01:09:40,360
The reason is…

808
01:09:40,510 --> 01:09:42,590
You're the one who did it.

809
01:09:47,450 --> 01:09:50,590
So then please tell me...

810
01:09:51,130 --> 01:09:54,830
How did I kidnap them both?

811
01:09:55,310 --> 01:09:58,300
As you wish.

812
01:09:59,980 --> 01:10:02,920
For the first case...

813
01:10:03,080 --> 01:10:06,940
...you set up a weight at the deck
behind the boat beforehand.

814
01:10:08,280 --> 01:10:10,380
Made a device that
will burn the rope...

815
01:10:10,620 --> 01:10:13,070
...and release the weight
when the time comes.

816
01:10:13,560 --> 01:10:18,960
And made it to look like
an outsider' job by putting traces...

817
01:10:19,240 --> 01:10:21,960
...that would look like
someone's hiding in the room.

818
01:10:22,620 --> 01:10:28,280
And to make it look like Sonoko was
thrown into the lake, you stole a life jacket.

819
01:10:34,860 --> 01:10:40,040
Then you placed a man's wetsuit,
oxygen tank and life jacket at the shore...

820
01:10:40,270 --> 01:10:43,840
...finishing your preparation.

821
01:10:48,480 --> 01:10:53,770
And on the day of crime,
you gave sleeping pills to Sonoko...

822
01:10:54,000 --> 01:10:57,070
...telling it her it was to help
with her seasickness.

823
01:10:58,280 --> 01:11:01,610
And you entered into the room
using the spare key you prepared earlier.

824
01:11:02,590 --> 01:11:05,980
And hid the sleeping Sonoko
somewhere.

825
01:11:10,320 --> 01:11:16,410
You took just the headband,
and using the device you made...

826
01:11:19,710 --> 01:11:24,940
...you threw it into the lake while
everyone was distracted by the sound.

827
01:11:33,070 --> 01:11:35,370
That's Sonoko's headband!

828
01:11:35,630 --> 01:11:40,360
And that is how you made it
look like Sonoko fell into the lake.

829
01:11:40,560 --> 01:11:42,060
Wait a moment.

830
01:11:42,490 --> 01:11:49,320
We searched the ship after that,
but Miss Sonoko was not there.

831
01:11:51,240 --> 01:11:54,970
It's not she was not there,
we just couldn't find her.

832
01:11:55,950 --> 01:11:58,380
Because of a simple trick.

833
01:11:59,390 --> 01:12:02,560
-Trick?
-A mirror.

834
01:12:03,960 --> 01:12:08,600
Back then, Sonoko was inside
the closet in the opposite room.

835
01:12:11,870 --> 01:12:14,030
It's a method frequently
used in magic tricks.

836
01:12:14,730 --> 01:12:18,680
By using the mirror's reflection...

837
01:12:18,880 --> 01:12:21,160
...it makes people think
there's nothing inside the closet.

838
01:12:21,880 --> 01:12:23,960
A very simple trick.

839
01:12:24,990 --> 01:12:28,360
After the police went out of the ship...

840
01:12:28,570 --> 01:12:34,960
...you removed the concealing mirror
and then truly kidnapped Sonoko.

841
01:12:38,320 --> 01:12:42,240
I found these, traces from the mirror.

842
01:12:42,880 --> 01:12:46,270
But anybody could do that,
not just me.

843
01:12:47,290 --> 01:12:53,340
And besides, during the second
kidnapping, I was outside all the time.

844
01:12:55,450 --> 01:12:59,440
Moreover, I was standing
right beside Mr. Kogoro Mori.

845
01:13:00,780 --> 01:13:06,110
At a glance, it seems
impossible for you to kidnap Ran.

846
01:13:07,180 --> 01:13:12,030
But, it's an easy thing to do
if you use that one method, right?

847
01:13:13,230 --> 01:13:15,360
Using that repulsive method.

848
01:13:20,400 --> 01:13:23,800
Ran… wasn't kidnapped.

849
01:13:25,710 --> 01:13:29,710
She left… on her own.

850
01:13:31,370 --> 01:13:36,010
You most probably slipped in
a threat letter to Ran.

851
01:13:36,760 --> 01:13:37,740
What's this?

852
01:13:37,880 --> 01:13:40,010
As well as the spare key
to Grand Hall.

853
01:13:47,360 --> 01:13:50,970
Sonoko Suzuki was kidnapped
by mistake instead of you.

854
01:13:53,690 --> 01:13:56,990
If you want to save her life...

855
01:13:57,180 --> 01:13:59,710
...leave the hall at noon.

856
01:14:00,170 --> 01:14:05,450
If you tell anyone,
Sonoko will be killed.

857
01:14:27,550 --> 01:14:32,750
And after that, you made her
to disguise herself as a hotel staff...

858
01:14:32,970 --> 01:14:35,390
...and told her to come here, right?

859
01:14:38,380 --> 01:14:43,500
Ran, who has a strong sense of justice
couldn't talk to even me about this matter.

860
01:14:44,040 --> 01:14:46,220
All by herself…

861
01:14:48,270 --> 01:14:54,350
To use her concern for her best friend
against her to commit your crimes...

862
01:14:54,640 --> 01:14:56,350
...you're the worse!

863
01:14:58,650 --> 01:15:02,760
Yes, Mr. Azuma is really the worst.

864
01:15:04,250 --> 01:15:06,190
He committed suicide, didn't he?

865
01:15:06,750 --> 01:15:08,560
I saw it on the news just now.

866
01:15:10,640 --> 01:15:12,270
Suicide?

867
01:15:13,480 --> 01:15:17,390
Was Azuma the one who did it?

868
01:15:18,060 --> 01:15:22,160
They found the will too,
so there's no mistaking it.

869
01:15:23,920 --> 01:15:25,800
You lost.

870
01:15:29,640 --> 01:15:33,370
You just admitted you did the crime.

871
01:15:34,240 --> 01:15:38,490
How did you know Azuma wrote a will?

872
01:15:39,180 --> 01:15:41,210
-I said I saw it on the news.
-No way!

873
01:15:41,710 --> 01:15:46,360
Because I took it
with me by mistake.

874
01:15:46,840 --> 01:15:48,970
Before the police got
to the crime scene.

875
01:15:49,420 --> 01:15:50,990
I just assumed it.

876
01:15:51,210 --> 01:15:54,320
It said it looked like suicide,
so I thought there must be a will.

877
01:15:54,440 --> 01:15:56,590
You really don't know
when to stop, do you?

878
01:15:56,800 --> 01:16:02,200
This will was written by Azuma,
after he was forced by the real culprit.

879
01:16:02,860 --> 01:16:06,640
And as proof...

880
01:16:06,840 --> 01:16:12,670
The real culprit's spelling is K-I-D-N-A-P-P-E-R.

881
01:16:12,860 --> 01:16:19,900
But Azuma's spelling was, K-I-D-N-A-P-E-R.

882
01:16:20,830 --> 01:16:22,760
It's missing one 'P'.

883
01:16:23,180 --> 01:16:25,580
They are both correct.

884
01:16:25,870 --> 01:16:30,250
But normally one person would not
use 2 ways to spell a word, right?

885
01:16:30,640 --> 01:16:36,040
And this will has clear proof
that you're the one who did it.

886
01:16:38,320 --> 01:16:41,720
The message Azume wrote
with everything he got.

887
01:16:42,090 --> 01:16:44,350
What message is that?

888
01:16:52,940 --> 01:16:57,070
A Kidnapper...Mai.

889
01:16:58,700 --> 01:17:01,400
The kidnapper is Mai.

890
01:17:02,270 --> 01:17:03,920
And that is you.

891
01:17:16,480 --> 01:17:19,310
So you must know this,
because you're here.

892
01:17:20,200 --> 01:17:24,400
The reason why
I sent you the challenge letter.

893
01:17:25,660 --> 01:17:30,170
You're the girlfriend of a man
I put behind bars...

894
01:17:30,320 --> 01:17:32,830
...after helping with
the investigation, in the past.

895
01:17:33,150 --> 01:17:37,440
That man was running
a wholesale company.

896
01:17:38,590 --> 01:17:42,540
But he started committing crime
after getting cornered by his debts.

897
01:17:45,080 --> 01:17:48,990
-And he died in prison.
-There's no time left.

898
01:17:49,500 --> 01:17:51,770
Where's Ran?

899
01:17:56,760 --> 01:18:00,520
You will not get away
even if you do that.

900
01:18:00,720 --> 01:18:03,200
I never intended
to run away for the start.

901
01:18:12,440 --> 01:18:14,250
Ran!

902
01:18:16,880 --> 01:18:19,450
Are you alright, Ran?

903
01:18:23,450 --> 01:18:25,290
Shinichi.

904
01:18:25,640 --> 01:18:29,950
You fool, you're too reckless.

905
01:18:32,140 --> 01:18:33,870
Sorry.

906
01:18:34,750 --> 01:18:37,120
Sorry for not realizing it sooner.

907
01:18:40,410 --> 01:18:46,380
This was your biggest SOS
sign to me, right?

908
01:19:14,190 --> 01:19:15,960
No.

909
01:19:17,630 --> 01:19:20,830
It was a sign to say that I believe you.

910
01:19:23,660 --> 01:19:26,220
I knew that you'd come.

911
01:19:32,480 --> 01:19:34,350
Ran!

912
01:19:39,100 --> 01:19:43,560
So, all 3 of us will die here.

913
01:19:58,960 --> 01:20:03,120
Ran, are you in there?
Ran!

914
01:20:07,840 --> 01:20:10,040
No use.

915
01:20:32,590 --> 01:20:34,650
Can you stop doing this?

916
01:20:36,730 --> 01:20:39,660
If you want to hate anyone,
hate you lover!

917
01:20:39,960 --> 01:20:43,150
-Don't bring us into this!
-It's true.

918
01:20:44,220 --> 01:20:46,640
He is the one at fault.

919
01:20:48,160 --> 01:20:51,680
But, I loved him.

920
01:20:53,230 --> 01:20:57,660
I had to hate someone
or I couldn't continue living.

921
01:20:59,370 --> 01:21:03,100
-This life without him.
-At least let Ran live.

922
01:21:04,780 --> 01:21:09,080
She's important to me,
more important than my life.

923
01:21:09,600 --> 01:21:11,980
You're important to her as well.

924
01:21:13,900 --> 01:21:18,190
So killing only you
would be cruel to her.

925
01:21:20,300 --> 01:21:28,520
If I let her live, all she can do to live
a life like a zombie, just like I did.

926
01:21:31,100 --> 01:21:34,440
-Ran is not weak.
-Are you sure?

927
01:21:36,000 --> 01:21:41,440
If you disappear, even she will…

928
01:21:44,120 --> 01:21:46,080
Both of you can't be separated.

929
01:21:48,270 --> 01:21:50,510
No matter what.

930
01:21:57,790 --> 01:21:59,980
Shinichi!

931
01:22:02,250 --> 01:22:04,120
Shinichi!

932
01:22:09,660 --> 01:22:11,720
This time…!

933
01:22:12,220 --> 01:22:14,040
Go!

934
01:22:14,220 --> 01:22:16,880
Thank you, Uncle.

935
01:22:26,320 --> 01:22:30,120
It's really the end, now.

936
01:23:00,440 --> 01:23:02,600
They are all white cables.

937
01:23:03,180 --> 01:23:04,570
Which one should I cut?

938
01:23:04,730 --> 01:23:10,190
I made it so no one can stop it.

939
01:23:12,720 --> 01:23:14,680
So…

940
01:23:15,500 --> 01:23:17,960
I don't know either.

941
01:23:37,230 --> 01:23:39,210
Shinichi?

942
01:23:39,480 --> 01:23:41,630
It's alright, Ran.

943
01:24:14,510 --> 01:24:17,870
And that is how the case is solved.

944
01:24:20,920 --> 01:24:22,240
Get in.

945
01:24:22,490 --> 01:24:24,910
-Let's go.
-Yes.

946
01:24:27,880 --> 01:24:31,930
Dad. I'm sorry.

947
01:24:33,230 --> 01:24:35,200
Don't say anything.

948
01:24:53,340 --> 01:24:55,150
Thank you.

949
01:24:56,200 --> 01:24:58,220
For saving Ran.

950
01:24:59,600 --> 01:25:02,220
It's all thanks to your assistance.

951
01:25:03,960 --> 01:25:05,370
Hmm!

952
01:25:06,860 --> 01:25:11,850
Both Ran, and Sonoko,
who was found nearby, was safe.

953
01:25:12,460 --> 01:25:14,140
Both of you!

954
01:25:14,480 --> 01:25:18,030
What are you thinking by taking
evidence away from the crime scene?

955
01:25:18,380 --> 01:25:21,500
You, you said you were
an inspector, right?

956
01:25:23,150 --> 01:25:25,130
You must say nonsense like that!

957
01:25:25,450 --> 01:25:29,180
But this case was solved
because of that will!

958
01:25:29,340 --> 01:25:31,440
That is a different topic than this!

959
01:25:31,680 --> 01:25:33,720
<i>Both of us were yelled at.</i>

960
01:25:36,430 --> 01:25:43,120
Ran's foot got better. She entered
the karate competition and won.

961
01:25:44,760 --> 01:25:49,120
And to celebrate, I was forced
to go to Tropical Land with her.

962
01:25:50,720 --> 01:25:55,310
That day would change my life,
and I had no idea.

963
01:25:58,410 --> 01:26:02,860
Hm, coming to
a theme park at this age.

964
01:26:07,980 --> 01:26:10,650
"The Cases of Sherlock Holmes"

965
01:26:12,160 --> 01:26:14,010
"Conan Doyle"

966
01:26:22,720 --> 01:26:27,690
-Hurry up, Mitsuhiko, Ayumi!
-Wait, Genta!

967
01:26:27,790 --> 01:26:30,800
You'll fall if you keep running like that!

968
01:26:31,950 --> 01:26:33,610
Ow, I fell on my face.

969
01:26:36,880 --> 01:26:39,130
Oh, you're here already.

970
01:26:42,510 --> 01:26:44,110
Let's go.

971
01:26:46,680 --> 01:26:48,360
Let's go to the roller coaster first.

972
01:26:49,360 --> 01:26:53,980
The last time we came, we were
around those kids' age, right?

973
01:26:54,330 --> 01:26:56,520
-Really?
-Yes!

974
01:26:56,640 --> 01:26:58,670
I was not that short.

975
01:26:59,420 --> 01:27:03,960
Let's go back to that time
and have some fun!

976
01:27:04,780 --> 01:27:06,660
Okay.

977
01:27:07,790 --> 01:27:10,720
Oh, right...!

978
01:27:10,910 --> 01:27:14,480
What were you
trying to tell me, back then?

979
01:27:14,730 --> 01:27:21,740
If I run away from this, he might do
something even worse the next time.

980
01:27:23,770 --> 01:27:26,990
And…

981
01:27:30,170 --> 01:27:32,410
-I forgot.
-Eh?

982
01:27:33,200 --> 01:27:35,880
It's nothing important.
Let's go.

983
01:27:36,330 --> 01:27:38,060
-Tell me.
-No way.

984
01:27:38,480 --> 01:27:40,650
And…

985
01:27:41,290 --> 01:27:43,980
I didn't want to worry you.

986
01:27:45,760 --> 01:27:50,750
Because you looked forward
to the school trip so much.

987
01:27:56,400 --> 01:27:58,760
While in Tropical Land with Ran...

988
01:27:58,890 --> 01:28:03,660
...I saw a group of suspicious men
in black and went after them.

989
01:28:04,030 --> 01:28:06,990
And that was the last time
I saw Ran as Shinichi.

990
01:28:07,960 --> 01:28:12,670
I was attacked by the men in black,
and when I was unconscious...

991
01:28:12,890 --> 01:28:15,160
...they made me
take an unknown drug.

992
01:28:16,270 --> 01:28:19,770
And when I woke up,
my body had been shrunken.

993
01:28:20,920 --> 01:28:23,520
My name is Shin…oh, no!

994
01:28:26,490 --> 01:28:29,600
Conan!
My name is Conan Edogawa!

